IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-convention-scope`
IMPORT `caa-convention-liability`
IMPORT `caa-convention-final`
IMPORT `caa-act`

-- INDEPENDENT tests for the Carriage by Air Act 1988.  Expected values were decided from
-- source/CAA1988.txt and encodings/BRIEF.md before any .l4 file was read.  A failing
-- assertion is a finding; none has been adjusted to fit the code.

`WS` MEANS `the Warsaw Convention`
`HG` MEANS `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention`
`MT` MEANS `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`

§ `A. Fixtures`

-- Ticket Facts positional: delivered, place/date, places, stopping, carrier name, statement,
-- single-HCP, indicates stop, notice, accepted/embarked without ticket
GIVEN `without` IS A BOOLEAN, `delivered` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Ticket Facts`
`tkt` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF delivered, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, notice, without

-- Baggage Check Facts positional (16): big, delivered, duplicate, place/date, places, name,
-- ticket no (d), bearer (e), number+weight (f), value (g), statement (h), combined, single HCP,
-- indicates stop, notice, took charge without check
GIVEN `big` IS A BOOLEAN, `without` IS A BOOLEAN, `delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `dd` IS A BOOLEAN, `ff` IS A BOOLEAN, `hh` IS A BOOLEAN, `other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `combined` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Baggage Check Facts`
`chk` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF big, delivered, other, other, other, other, dd, other, ff, other, hh, combined, FALSE, FALSE, notice, without

-- Waybill Facts positional (30)
GIVEN `without` IS A BOOLEAN, `made` IS A BOOLEAN, `ai` IS A BOOLEAN, `q` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `jp` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Waybill Facts`
`wb` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF made, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, jp, jp, jp, jp, jp, jp, jp, q, FALSE, FALSE, notice, TRUE, FALSE, without

-- Limit Facts positional (9): higher agreed, higher, declared?, declared sum, carrier proves greater,
-- actual interest, weight, affects other packages, other weight
`lf plain` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 20, FALSE, 0
`lf higher` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF TRUE, 300_000, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE, 0
`lf cargo 100kg` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 100, FALSE, 0
`lf declared` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, TRUE, 40_000, FALSE, 0, 100, FALSE, 0
`lf declared but greater than interest` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, TRUE, 40_000, TRUE, 30_000, 100, FALSE, 0
`lf part affecting others` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 10, TRUE, 5
`lf part alone` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, 10, FALSE, 5

§ `B. Article 22, limits (each text its own)`

#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 125_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for cargo`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for cargo`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 17
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for cargo`)'s `the unit` EQUALS `Special Drawing Rights`
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT NOT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` WS `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` HG `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` MT `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 5_000

-- amounts
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf plain` EQUALS 125_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf plain` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf plain` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf higher` EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf higher` EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons` `lf higher` EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for registered baggage` `lf plain` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for registered baggage` `lf plain` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for registered baggage` `lf plain` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for cargo` `lf cargo 100kg` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for cargo` `lf cargo 100kg` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for cargo` `lf cargo 100kg` EQUALS 1_700
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for cargo` `lf declared` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for cargo` `lf declared` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for cargo` `lf declared` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for cargo` `lf declared but greater than interest` EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for cargo` `lf declared but greater than interest` EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself` `lf plain` EQUALS 5_000
-- weight rule for part loss (First 22(2)(b), Third 22(2)(c)); Second has none
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for cargo` `lf part affecting others` EQUALS 3_750
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for registered baggage` `lf part affecting others` EQUALS 3_750
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` HG `the liability for cargo` `lf part alone` EQUALS 2_500
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` MT `the liability for cargo` `lf part alone` EQUALS 170
#ASSERT `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for cargo` `lf part alone` EQUALS 2_500
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount to which the carrier's liability is limited` WS `the liability for cargo` `lf part affecting others`

§ `C. Article 22(4), costs`

-- occurrence 10 Jan 2025; action commenced 1 Sep 2025 (later than the six months, 10 Jul 2025)
`costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages = offer` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_000, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 9 1, JUST (YMD 2025 7 10)
`costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages above offer` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_001, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 9 1, JUST (YMD 2025 7 10)
`costs, offer on 11 Jul before action` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_000, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 9 1, JUST (YMD 2025 7 11)
`costs, offer on the day of action` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_000, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 9 1, JUST (YMD 2025 9 1)
-- action commenced early (1 May 2025): six months (10 Jul) is later
`costs, early action, offer 10 Jul` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_000, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 5 1, JUST (YMD 2025 7 10)
`costs, early action, offer 11 Jul` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 60_000, JUST 60_000, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 5 1, JUST (YMD 2025 7 11)
`costs, no offer` MEANS `Costs Facts` OF 10, NOTHING, YMD 2025 1 10, YMD 2025 9 1, NOTHING

#ASSERT `the carrier's offer was made in time` `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages = offer`
#ASSERT `the carrier's offer was made in time` `costs, offer on 11 Jul before action`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier's offer was made in time` `costs, offer on the day of action`
#ASSERT `the carrier's offer was made in time` `costs, early action, offer 10 Jul`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier's offer was made in time` `costs, early action, offer 11 Jul`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` HG `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages = offer`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` MT `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages = offer`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` HG `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages above offer`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` MT `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages above offer`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` HG `costs, offer on the day of action`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` MT `costs, early action, offer 11 Jul`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` HG `costs, no offer`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` WS `costs, offer on 10 Jul, damages = offer`

§ `D. Article 26, complaint periods; s 7`

-- kind, receipt, discovery, complaint date, forthwith, in writing, fraud
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of Complaint`, `made` IS A DATE, `forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN, `writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Complaint Facts`
`cf` MEANS `Complaint Facts` OF k, YMD 2025 3 1, YMD 2025 3 1, made, forthwith, writing, fraud

-- Warsaw: baggage 3, cargo 7, delay 14
#ASSERT `the last day for the complaint` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 4) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 4
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 4) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 9) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 16) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 16) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Hague: 7, 14, 21
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 9) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 16) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 22) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 23) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 22) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 23) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Montreal: 7, 14, 21
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 8) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 9) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 16) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 22) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `delay of baggage` (YMD 2025 3 23) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 22) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` MT (`cf` `delay of cargo` (YMD 2025 3 23) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- the same date is in time under one text and late under another
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 6) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 6) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- forthwith, writing, fraud (26(3), (4))
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 5) FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the complaint was made in time` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 5) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `an action lies against the carrier` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an action lies against the carrier` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 20) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `an action lies against the carrier` HG (`cf` `damage to cargo` (YMD 2025 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `an action lies against the carrier` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an action lies against the carrier` WS (`cf` `damage to baggage` (YMD 2025 3 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 7: receipt of the remainder where part is lost
`part lost` MEANS `Partial Loss Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2025 3 10, YMD 2025 3 1
`nothing lost` MEANS `Partial Loss Facts` OF FALSE, YMD 2025 3 10, YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `the date of receipt for Article 26(2)` `part lost` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 10
#ASSERT `the date of receipt for Article 26(2)` `nothing lost` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `for Article 26(2) damage includes loss of part of the baggage or cargo`

§ `E. Documents of carriage: forfeiture (Arts 3, 4, 9)`

-- Passenger ticket
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` WS (`tkt` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` HG (`tkt` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` MT (`tkt` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` WS (`tkt` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` HG (`tkt` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` MT (`tkt` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` WS (`tkt` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` HG (`tkt` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` MT (`tkt` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`

-- Baggage check: chk big without delivered dd ff hh other combined notice
-- Warsaw: only (d), (f), (h) missing, or no check, forfeits
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
-- small personal objects need no check
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` WS (`chk` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
-- Hague / Montreal: forfeit 22(2) only
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` HG (`chk` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` MT (`chk` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` HG (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` MT (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` HG (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` MT (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` HG (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` MT (`chk` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`

-- Air waybill: wb without made ai q notice jp
-- Warsaw 9: no waybill, or any of (a)-(i) or (q) missing, forfeits; (j)-(p) do not
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` WS (`wb` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` WS (`wb` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` WS (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` WS (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` WS (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
-- Hague 9: no waybill (with consent) or no Art 8(c) notice forfeits 22(2)
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` HG (`wb` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` HG (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` HG (`wb` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
-- Montreal 9: non-compliance never affects limitation
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` MT (`wb` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` MT (`wb` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
-- absence of documents never affects validity of the contract
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the passenger ticket affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the baggage check affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the air waybill affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`

§ `F. Documents: text-specific provisions (REFUSE where a text is silent)`

#ASSERT `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` WS
#ASSERT `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` HG
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` MT
#ASSERT REFUSED `nothing in the Convention prevents the issue of a negotiable air waybill` WS
#ASSERT `nothing in the Convention prevents the issue of a negotiable air waybill` HG
#ASSERT REFUSED `nothing in the Convention prevents the issue of a negotiable air waybill` MT
#ASSERT REFUSED `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` WS
#ASSERT REFUSED `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` HG
#ASSERT NOT `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` MT
#ASSERT REFUSED `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` WS
#ASSERT `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` HG
#ASSERT `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` MT
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` WS (`Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` HG (`Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` WS (`Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` HG (`Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` MT (`Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` WS TRUE (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` HG TRUE (`wb` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `G. Articles 18, 20, 21 (defences)`

-- Defence Facts: measures, impossible, pilotage, other respects
`measures` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`impossible` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`nothing proved` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`pilotage and others` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`pilotage only` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

`pax` MEANS `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger`
`bag` MEANS `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage`
`cgo` MEANS `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo`
`dly` MEANS `delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo`

#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `pax` `measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `pax` `impossible`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `pax` `nothing proved`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `cgo` `pilotage and others`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `bag` `pilotage and others`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `cgo` `pilotage only`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` WS `pax` `pilotage and others`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` HG `cgo` `pilotage and others`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` HG `bag` `pilotage and others`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` HG `cgo` `measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` HG `pax` `impossible`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `pax` `measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `bag` `impossible`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `dly` `measures`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `cgo` `measures`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `cgo` `impossible`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` MT `bag` `pilotage and others`

-- Cargo Loss Facts (11): baggage dmg, cargo dmg, during carriage, in charge, land/sea, in performance,
-- proof contrary, inherent, packaging, war, public authority
`cargo lost` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely by war` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely by inherent vice` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely by packaging` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely by public authority` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`baggage lost, inherent vice flag` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo not during carriage` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
